      "type": "title",
      "headline": "How a policy engine fences an agent",
      "sub": "An open agent loop, and a sandbox that only lets policy out.",
      "punch": [
        "Real shell.",
        "Hidden keys.",
        "Rules with memory."
      ],
      "say": "Hi, I'm Tether! An open agent framework from Amazon, and a new sandbox that wraps any agent in rules."
    },
    {
      "type": "idea",
      "text": "The kernel sandbox decides almost nothing. It makes the policy layer the only way out, so every action is judged where it still has meaning.",
      "mark": "the only way out",
      "say": "The idea. The kernel sandbox only funnels. Every way out runs through one policy engine."
    },
    {
